# Laravel Project Rules for Cursor IDE

## 1. CORS HEADERS - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
- NEVER add CORS headers in multiple places (index.php, middleware, controllers)
- Use ONLY the AddCorsHeaders middleware for CORS
- Always check if headers already exist before adding: `if (!$response->headers->has('Access-Control-Allow-Origin'))`
- CORS headers MUST be added to ALL responses, including error responses (500, 404, 422)
- Handle OPTIONS preflight requests immediately in middleware, return 200/204
- Test CORS in browser, not just curl (curl doesn't enforce CORS)



## ADDITIONAL GUIDELINES
- Keep solutions simple - avoid overengineering
- Follow existing code patterns in the project
- Test endpoints with curl before assuming they work
- When fixing errors, ensure CORS headers are still present
- Use consistent file/folder naming conventions
- Document complex logic with comments
- Prefer Laravel's built-in features over custom solutions when possible

